            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a stranger, then the Malayalam for a party."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കല",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കല — kala — \"art\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കല (kala) is Sanskrit kalā, \"any practical art\" (CDIAL 2927). CDIAL takes the Sanskrit word itself from Dravidian, and DEDR 1297 sets it beside Tamil kal, \"to learn\", so the word may have come home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
